---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const entries = [
  { v: '1.4 of The Reality Code Engine (site)', date: '14 October 2026', items: [
    'One RCE playground: the reference checker in the browser at openie-dev.github.io/rce is the RCE playground. The engine demo (intent to Form, gate, proof replay, interfaces, compounding, energy) moved from /playground/rce/ to /demos/rce-engine/, and the old address redirects there with its anchor, so links in earlier PDFs still land on the same layer.',
    'The paper, its translations, the LaTeX PDF, the home page, llms.txt and the WebMCP tools link the playground and the engine demo by these names.',
  ]},
  { v: '1.4 of The Reality Code Engine', date: '13 October 2026', items: [
    'Engine test count corrected to 589 distinct tests (cargo test --release at 1eb5f02; 0 failures, 2 ignored). Version 1.3 printed 596, the make check total, which runs 7 proof tests twice.',
    'Section 3.7: specification 2.7 now states the per-call-site cost rule of C.15 (openIE-dev/rce ac94a8f); /rce/spec/ regenerated.',
    'Section 5.5: the deterministic proposer offered 87 identities (77 arithmetic, 10 structural); 9 admitted, 78 rejected, from the engine test tests/form_proposers.rs.',
    'Section 7: Software Heritage and Rosetta Code cited as [129] to [131]; archive counters reread (30.3 billion file contents, 448 million origins).',
    'Nine figures added (Figures 5 to 10, 12, 13 and 15); earlier Figures 5 and 6 renumbered 11 and 14. Translations, including German, remain at version 1.1.',
    'Site: new Opportunity map page with three boards and their sources.',
  ]},
  { v: '1.1', date: '11 October 2026', items: [
    'All papers: version and revision date under the title.',
    'The Reality Code Engine: rule-authoring timeline against the corpus freeze (corpus20 is a development set); n and a 95% interval on the headline result; gross beside idle-subtracted RAPL joules; host described as an x86 laptop; Section 5.1 renamed to differential testing; scope of the ASM theorem stated, with the Form as a modelling choice; repair, overfitting and benchmark-bias lineage; held-out and baseline protocols (8.4, 8.5); Falsifiers, Work to finish and Conclusion sections.',
    'The Promised Trillion Dollar AI-Coding Market: McKinsey, Goldman Sachs, GitHub, Gartner, Sequoia and Stargate rows; productivity evidence table; Microsoft pre-tax and net figures; Cursor repricing; the 9 to 900 times price range, LLMflation and the DeepSeek cut; bundling by the platform owner; the price elasticity; coverage proposition E5; conditional conclusion.',
    'Thermodynamic Bounds (agency): the thesis read through its gate, against Burnell, Zhou, Laber and existing gated metrics; objections to the floor (Section 3.0); Koyuk and Seifert for driven acts; Jordan on Margolus-Levitin; the estimator replacement; falsifier outcomes in Section 5.2; the Sudoku grid stated as inside the agent wall.',
    'Metered Commit Gates: KV260 figures relabeled SOM-level with the rail cited, seed-fabric result marked inconclusive; runtime-enforcement lineage; cascade lineage; II.3 renamed cost model.',
    'Task Satiation: sections renumbered (old 2.8 to 2.10 and 3.6 to 3.8 are now 3.6 to 3.11, with the old anchors kept); rebound canon; predicate endogeneity; H1 from public trajectories; tokens and joules; identification limits.',
    'Spell Check is Global: title tidied; the few stated as a price class; connected reach from ITU; premium tier moved up a layer; bundling economics; grammatical error correction and the energy trade-off.',
    'Site: navigation and footer list every paper and PDF; one measured_j definition; nine glossary terms; one Notational Intelligence definition; About count; catalog hero wording.',
  ]},
];
---
<Layout title="Changelog | OpenIE Research" description="Dated revisions of the OpenIE research papers.">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-white">Changelog</h1>
    {entries.map((e) => (
      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-brand-white">Version {e.v}, {e.date}</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
          {e.items.map((i) => <li class="mt-2">{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </main>
</Layout>
